# Used automatically by `npm run build` (Vite reads .env.production for a
# production build). Dev is unaffected - that still uses .env.
#
# Relative on purpose. In the bundle Django serves both the app and the API
# from one origin, so the frontend must not name a host or port: the clinic PC
# may serve on localhost, on its LAN address, or on a different port, and an
# absolute URL baked in at build time would break all but one of those.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
